    pr_ref:  # 571b
    description: ""  # 571b
    fields:  # 571b
      statement: "When 'hypergumbo verify-claims' is given --taint-sources / --taint-sinks / --taint-sanitizers PATH and that path is nonexistent, malformed YAML, or wrong-shape content, the command must error out (or at minimum print a warning) — not silently report 'All N claim(s) CONFIRMED' with exit 0."  # 571b
      root_cause: "The taint-flag file loaders fall back to empty catalog on any failure (including FileNotFoundError, YAMLError, schema mismatch). Combined with INV-mofih (verify-claims accepts unknown/missing claim type as confirmed), a user can mis-spell their entire taint configuration AND get 'All CONFIRMED' with zero indication anything went wrong. Tested: --taint-sources nonexistent.yml → confirmed; --taint-sources <random_text>.yml → confirmed; --taint-sinks bad.json → confirmed. Strengthens INV-mofih severity argument — verify-claims is fail-silent on essentially every input failure mode on the security-critical command."  # 571b
